Of course. The wretched of the earth. Yeah. How can we take inspiration? All of that kind of somebody would bring along a dogged copy of France Fanon and Albert Camus. No question whatsoever. But there would be a hard-faced man in the corner who's no strange to blowing up a post office, that kind of thing. And it was actually from the wolf-ta... own societies that the idea of a big civil rights campaign really took off. And when you look at the first meeting of this NICRA, Northern Ireland's civil rights association, when you look at who was there at the first meeting, yeah, there are a load of people who like civil liberties and are members of like a Labour Party this and a Labour Party that or whatever, but there are

