1967, 68, precisely the point when the traditional industries on which Northern Ireland depends are in real trouble, the jobs are drying up. The working class Protestants that probably you do need to persuade are frightened about economic and cultural change. So it's much more difficult. If you've come back from the shipyard, you're worried your job's going to go. when you open the newspaper and you see a load of people are complaining about something, effectively you have to make the concession, it's much harder to do, I would say.

