who are very defensive, indeed, outraged, when they hear about Catholics saying they are second-class citizens. Our housing was the same as our Catholic next-door neighbor, two up, two down, with an outside toilet. It really irks me when I hear about the disadvantages that the Catholics had. Protestantism and unionism in Northern Ireland, it's not a monolith. There are a lot of very poor people who are part of that community. And they feel, you know, when they're told, oh, you are the first class citizens,

