and then there are kind of copycat riots across Northern Ireland watching all this from Belfast Terence O'Neill knows that he has to do something and five days after he says to his cabinet, he meets his cabinet, he says, I'm going to go to London, I'm going to see Harold Wilson, and I know that Harold Wilson is going to ask me for some pretty big changes.

