the home office, they gave him a huge sort of briefing document. There's lots of stuff about prisons, race relations, the fire service, the police, and there was nothing in this document about Northern Ireland at all. There isn't at this point a secretary of state for Northern Ireland? No, no, no, no, no. We don't need one because it's being run from Belfast. However, Wilson and Callahan are interested now because there's a lot of fighting. You know, there's been this business in dairy. They can see there's a problem. But at the end of 1968, they've got a problem.

