I mean, just to remind people, this is a guy who'd fought in the Second World War and taken out tank proteins, I imagine. Most people in their story have some sort of war. I mean, it's always the way with 60s and 70s, UK history, isn't it? Set for Jerry Adams. Yes, yes. Well, Amy Pace didn't advise in the war. No doubt made warlike speeches, but I don't think he took out a German machine gun nest or anything like that. It's the shabby men in London, isn't it? Who did that?

