So Spain has not been involved in the First World War at all. It's been a backwater. Basically, it's been really politically turbulent. There is a king. It's normally a parliamentary system. Most of Spain is untouched by the modern world. So it feels like these these huge estates called the Latifundiae, which go back to the Roman period. I found this extraordinary. I had no idea until I started reading up for the second. Well, this is true of Spain and Portugal, actually. They would have absolutely gigantic rural

