01:16:54.000 --> 01:17:32.000
estate run by landowners, almost going to feudal system. The peasants are enthralled to the landowner and to the church and whatnot. There are parts of Spain that have industrialized, the Basque Country, the North and Catalonia, but those are obviously places with separatist movements. So Spain feels very fractured, and there's lots of labour unrest, there's a big anarchist movement, there was a socialist movement, there was a communist party. In the 20s, there was a coup and a general took power called General Miguel Primo de Rivera, under the king. But that didn't really work out.

